           Upstream now does officially what patch items 5 and part of 2 do by hand,
           and community-1 is the upstream default for --diarize_model.
  7892a72  Optimize assign_word_speakers with interval tree for 228x speedup
           Replaces the O(n) scan. This deletes the reason patch item 6 exists.
           On a nine-hour file this is the difference between a long wait and none.
  c8f7597  feat: add hotwords argument to CLI
           --hotwords biases decoding toward rare terms. This is upstream of the whole
           transcript-fixes.tsv spelling pipeline: Ca'armine, Shasherak, Alekeemo,
           Ghanil, Nalcir, Zrithrak, Drennos, Tarkus Vell, Aedelfred. NOT available on
           3.4.2, which is why step 3 above uses --initial_prompt instead. --initial_prompt
           only conditions the first window; --hotwords applies throughout.
  d00ec69  feat: add progress_callback to transcribe, align, and diarize
  f2609a6  fix: revert #986 wildcard alignment that broke word-level timestamps
  39aa9f5  fix: restore word-level timestamps for unalignable characters
  c4c1242  fix: derive SRT/VTT cue times from word-level timestamps
           Three timestamp-correctness fixes. Every codex citation is a timestamp.
  064f737  fix: default compute_type to float32 on CPU
           Makes --compute_type float32 redundant.
  570b08b  fix: add no_repeat_ngram_size and repetition_penalty options
           Useful against Whisper repetition loops.
  db317c3  feat: add language-aware sentence tokenization
  1baf8d2  feat: pass --hf_token to WhisperModel for gated model support
  6ec4a02  chore: drop python 3.9 support   /   d13171c  feat: support python 3.13

New CLI flags at v3.8.6 that do not exist locally: --hotwords, --log-level,
--compute_type default.

BEFORE YOU PULL, READ THIS:
  - v3.8.6 has NO --output_format spk. Its choices are all/srt/vtt/txt/tsv/json/aud.
    Pulling without re-applying WriteSPK breaks the codex pipeline completely.
  - v3.8.6 has NO --diarize_from_json, NO mps handling (its --device help says
    "e.g. cpu, cuda"; passing mps would go straight to CTranslate2), NO exact-count
    behaviour, and NO pre-diarization checkpoint.
  - v3.8.6 is hard-committed to pyannote 4: it reads output.speaker_diarization with no
    3.x fallback. Upgrading whisperX REQUIRES doing the pyannote 4 step first.
  - ONE PLACE THE LOCAL PATCH IS BETTER THAN UPSTREAM: upstream uses
    output.speaker_diarization; the local patch prefers output.exclusive_speaker_diarization.
    The exclusive annotation has no overlapping turns, which is what you want when
    assigning one speaker per transcript segment. Keep this when rebasing.

SUGGESTED ORDER:
  1. uv add "pyannote.audio>=4.0" and verify the version sticks after `uv run`.
  2. Re-run an already-hand-checked file with --diarize_from_json and --diarize_model
     pyannote/speaker-diarization-community-1. Compare against the known-good labels
     before trusting it on anything new. 2024_01_05_dyingGrove is the right test case:
     it is short, and its documented failure is exactly the one VBx should fix.
  3. Only then rebase the five-file patch onto v3.8.6, keeping items 1-4 and the
     exclusive-annotation choice, and DROPPING item 6 (upstream is 228x faster) and the
     3.x compatibility half of item 5.
